WEBVTT

00:12.012 --> 00:13.722
EDUCATIONAL RIGHTS PROTECTION BUREAU

00:13.805 --> 00:15.807
ALL REPORTS
ARE KEPT CONFIDENTIAL AS A RULE

00:15.890 --> 00:18.685
PLEASE HELP OUR SCHOOL
THIS JUST ISN'T RIGHT

00:18.768 --> 00:20.395
THIS IS DAILY LIFE AT OUR SCHOOL

00:20.478 --> 00:21.730
IT'S REALLY MESSED UP

00:21.813 --> 00:22.939
PLEASE COME HELP, ERPB

00:26.151 --> 00:28.653
I FEEL SO BAD FOR OUR TEACHER

00:34.993 --> 00:36.953
EXPOSING THE STUDENT
WHO ASSAULTED A TEACHER

00:37.454 --> 00:39.330
REPORTING A SERIOUS ASSAULT ON A TEACHER

00:48.548 --> 00:50.967
You will remember
the death of a female teacher

00:51.051 --> 00:53.511
that led to the establishment of the ERPB.

00:54.012 --> 00:57.307
The current Minister of Education
and head of the ERPB, Choi Gang-seok,

00:58.725 --> 01:01.061
is the victim's father.

01:02.479 --> 01:05.106
And Inspector Na Hwa-jin was her fiancé.

01:07.984 --> 01:08.902
Is it truly possible

01:08.985 --> 01:13.156
this has nothing to do with
the teacher killed by her student?

01:13.865 --> 01:16.826
These people are not working
for educational rights.

01:17.535 --> 01:18.870
It is cruel revenge

01:18.953 --> 01:21.498
for the death
of their daughter and fiancée.

01:22.373 --> 01:24.000
It is a personal vendetta.

01:29.089 --> 01:30.006
Im Han-rim.

01:32.634 --> 01:33.593
What are you doing?

01:34.344 --> 01:35.762
Have you eaten, sir?

01:35.845 --> 01:36.679
Yeah.

01:37.847 --> 01:38.765
Let's go.

01:38.848 --> 01:40.600
Did you happen to see

01:41.601 --> 01:42.811
the press conference?

01:48.358 --> 01:49.400
Yeah.

01:53.404 --> 01:54.948
Is it all true?

01:55.657 --> 01:56.991
Yes, it's true.

02:04.332 --> 02:07.043
You'll be late to the meeting
if you just stand there.

02:07.544 --> 02:08.586
Come on, hurry.

02:13.174 --> 02:15.510
We have a lot to do.
Where the hell did everyone go?

02:20.765 --> 02:23.268
They're eccentric and…

02:23.977 --> 02:26.855
The members' eccentric,

02:27.564 --> 02:30.066
ignorant, and tyrannical…

02:30.775 --> 02:34.863
I do not see any potential for improvement

02:35.363 --> 02:37.657
in team members' capabilities--

02:37.740 --> 02:40.201
"Therefore, I am requesting
a transfer of assignment."

02:40.827 --> 02:42.787
Gosh, this is…

02:42.871 --> 02:44.789
ASSIGNMENT TRANSFER APPLICATION

02:48.168 --> 02:49.419
Deputy Bong Geun-dae.

02:50.211 --> 02:51.212
Yes, sir.

02:51.296 --> 02:53.173
What is this font?

02:54.007 --> 02:55.175
It's so eye-catching.

02:56.342 --> 02:57.177
Pardon?

02:57.260 --> 02:59.971
Let's use this font
for all official documents from now on.

03:05.518 --> 03:06.394
Oh, yes.

03:07.061 --> 03:08.563
By the way,

03:10.148 --> 03:11.858
that's not a good enough reason.

03:12.567 --> 03:15.904
If you want to be reassigned,
give me a convincing reason.

03:15.987 --> 03:19.240
A reason I can't logically argue against
in any way.

03:19.782 --> 03:23.036
Otherwise, it comes across as whining
to people like us.

03:25.747 --> 03:26.581
Hello, sir.

03:26.664 --> 03:28.958
We're so damn busy right now.
Get a move on!

03:29.042 --> 03:30.293
Look at the time!

03:35.632 --> 03:36.466
Safe…

03:45.558 --> 03:48.686
This report is about

03:48.770 --> 03:52.273
the assault of a teacher by a male student

03:52.857 --> 03:55.485
at Chukmyeong Foreign Language High.

03:55.568 --> 03:57.362
This is the teacher on the screen.

03:57.445 --> 04:01.699
The informant is a colleague
of the assaulted teacher.

04:01.783 --> 04:05.328
They also sent a video of the incident.

04:05.411 --> 04:07.121
-Play the video.
-Yes, sir.

04:10.208 --> 04:11.125
Park Hyeon-ung!

04:11.209 --> 04:12.835
What the hell are you doing?

04:12.919 --> 04:15.463
All that praise
has gone to your head, hasn't it?

04:19.509 --> 04:20.843
Mr. Cheon, are you okay?

04:20.927 --> 04:23.346
-Are you out of your mind?
-Hey, what's wrong?

04:23.429 --> 04:25.556
-What is it?
-Hyeon-ung, what's gotten into you?

04:26.057 --> 04:27.183
Stop it.

04:32.438 --> 04:35.358
TEACH YOU A LESSON

04:35.441 --> 04:38.319
CHUKMYEONG FOREIGN LANGUAGE HIGH SCHOOL

04:38.403 --> 04:40.488
Wow. Is this a school?

04:40.989 --> 04:43.491
What kind of high school looks like this?

04:44.200 --> 04:45.034
I know, right?

04:45.660 --> 04:49.539
I heard they're the best of their kind.
They're very flashy.

04:50.415 --> 04:53.501
You guys go ahead.
I'll catch up with you shortly, all right?

04:55.003 --> 04:55.878
Let's go.

04:57.338 --> 05:00.008
Grades alone don't guarantee
college entry anymore.

05:00.091 --> 05:01.884
-Especially Seoul National Uni.
-Yes.

05:01.968 --> 05:04.804
When I saw his student records,
he had public speaking…

05:04.887 --> 05:07.223
Chukmyeong Foreign Language High School

05:07.307 --> 05:11.477
actually had a lower profile
than other foreign language high schools.

05:11.978 --> 05:14.647
But after that teacher, Mr. Cheon,
started working here,

05:15.231 --> 05:20.445
more students got into elite colleges,
and this became an elite high school.

05:20.528 --> 05:22.989
-It's because they worked so hard.
-But you weren't…

05:23.072 --> 05:24.907
Is that how he became famous?

05:24.991 --> 05:27.744
It was more because of his character.

05:28.244 --> 05:30.997
He's actually really famous
for being a true educator.

05:31.581 --> 05:32.665
A true educator?

05:34.375 --> 05:35.877
Why would a kid hit him?

05:35.960 --> 05:37.337
You're amazing, seriously.

05:38.046 --> 05:39.172
Gosh, sir.

05:39.672 --> 05:41.883
I'd always hoped to meet you one day.

05:41.966 --> 05:45.678
If I ever had the chance to do so,
I wanted to say thank you.

05:45.762 --> 05:46.596
Right.

05:48.014 --> 05:50.058
Allow me
to formally introduce myself, sir.

05:50.141 --> 05:54.228
My name is Na Hwa-jin.
I'm an inspector from the ERPB.

05:54.312 --> 05:55.188
Right, hello.

05:55.271 --> 05:57.857
I got into the Korea Military Academy

05:57.940 --> 06:00.276
after listening
to your EBS online lectures.

06:00.360 --> 06:03.571
That wouldn't be down to me.
You must have worked very hard for it.

06:03.654 --> 06:07.825
The things you said
now and then during your lectures…

06:07.909 --> 06:08.910
The…

06:09.786 --> 06:11.662
Gosh, this is just…

06:11.746 --> 06:12.997
-Are you all right?
-Wow.

06:13.539 --> 06:16.501
What's happening?
What's wrong with Inspector Na?

06:16.584 --> 06:18.002
What you said was really…

06:32.016 --> 06:33.393
Inspector, can't we just

06:34.227 --> 06:35.353
forget this happened?

06:36.187 --> 06:37.730
We have midterm exams soon.

06:37.814 --> 06:40.316
They're important
to Hyeon-ung and the other students.

06:40.400 --> 06:43.945
But still, he was in the wrong
and should be punished.

06:50.243 --> 06:51.744
Sir,

06:51.828 --> 06:54.622
could I perhaps ask a big favor?

06:55.790 --> 06:56.624
Yes, sure.

06:56.707 --> 06:59.669
You know your sign-off
at the end of your online lectures?

06:59.752 --> 07:02.004
Could you say it just one more time?

07:02.088 --> 07:03.756
"I believe in your potential."

07:04.340 --> 07:06.008
Oh my gosh.

07:06.676 --> 07:11.347
There just so happens to be a blackboard
and chalk right here, so…

07:11.848 --> 07:14.142
May I please ask you to do it?

07:14.225 --> 07:16.185
Gosh, Inspector.

07:20.565 --> 07:22.650
I believe in your potential.

07:42.211 --> 07:43.421
Wow!

07:44.046 --> 07:47.091
-You can't just touch it like that.
-What is all this?

07:47.175 --> 07:49.635
I bought it with my most recent paycheck.

07:49.719 --> 07:52.388
Believe it or not, it's dual monitors.

07:52.472 --> 07:54.390
It has a touchscreen,

07:54.474 --> 07:57.059
and the mounting bracket at the back
comes in handy.

07:57.560 --> 07:58.978
Right, it's a computer.

08:00.021 --> 08:03.357
It's not just any computer.
It's a portable monitor.

08:03.441 --> 08:05.693
The display is 16:9, and it's full HD.

08:05.776 --> 08:09.405
It's 15.6 inches, which is great
for watching Netflix and movies.

08:09.489 --> 08:12.617
And it's optimized for gaming
with the ideal aspect ratio and size.

08:14.243 --> 08:15.912
And see this small thing here?

08:15.995 --> 08:17.163
The white USB-C port.

08:17.246 --> 08:21.792
This single device can supply power
and support display output simultaneously.

08:23.169 --> 08:24.337
So it's expensive.

08:27.632 --> 08:28.466
Nice.

08:32.803 --> 08:36.599
PATIENCE

08:50.780 --> 08:52.782
Are you Park Hyeon-ung?

08:56.494 --> 08:59.539
You assaulted your teacher, Mr. Cheon,
a few days ago.

08:59.622 --> 09:00.790
What was the reason?

09:03.501 --> 09:05.545
If I tell you,
will you let me off the hook?

09:06.796 --> 09:08.047
No, you won't!

09:08.881 --> 09:11.551
Expel me or report me to the police
if you want.

09:11.634 --> 09:13.803
Don't pretend you want to know.

09:19.475 --> 09:21.310
If it's hard to decide,

09:21.394 --> 09:23.813
should I make it easy for you?

09:30.278 --> 09:33.072
Do not make me write
the Chinese character for "patience."

09:35.908 --> 09:40.663
The school still hasn't decided
how to punish that kid, Park Hyeon-ung.

09:40.746 --> 09:44.041
I thought the ERPB could really show them,

09:44.125 --> 09:45.835
so I reported the incident.

09:46.836 --> 09:50.756
Mr. Cheon is like a role model
to many other teachers.

09:51.882 --> 09:55.553
He makes you want to become more like him.

09:56.637 --> 10:01.017
Our school didn't attain elite status
simply because he teaches well.

10:01.100 --> 10:05.062
Mr. Cheon is someone
who stays up all night with the students

10:05.146 --> 10:08.691
and gets more excited than they do
when they are accepted into college.

10:08.774 --> 10:11.319
Once the news spread,
students poured in to enroll.

10:12.820 --> 10:14.905
To hit a teacher like him…

10:14.989 --> 10:17.950
I couldn't just stand by and do nothing.

10:19.869 --> 10:20.870
I see.

10:33.549 --> 10:34.508
Damn it!

10:39.180 --> 10:41.390
When do boys usually hit puberty?

10:41.474 --> 10:43.184
Generally, as hormones change,

10:43.267 --> 10:46.270
it spans from middle school
to the second year of high school.

10:46.354 --> 10:48.105
So he's probably at the end of it.

10:48.189 --> 10:49.815
He's all bravado and rage.

10:49.899 --> 10:53.778
He utterly refuses to listen,
and I bet his grades are utterly bad.

10:53.861 --> 10:56.280
Don't make hasty generalizations…

10:56.364 --> 10:59.200
I mean, I think you're mistaken.

10:59.867 --> 11:00.701
About what?

11:01.952 --> 11:02.787
Park Hyeon-ung.

11:04.789 --> 11:06.457
He's ranked first in his grade.

11:07.500 --> 11:08.542
STUDENT REPORT CARD

11:10.336 --> 11:11.337
He really is.

11:11.420 --> 11:12.922
So why would he…

11:13.923 --> 11:15.216
He's ranked first.

11:15.716 --> 11:17.051
Why would he do it?

11:25.226 --> 11:27.061
EXAM MANAGEMENT OFFICE

11:29.480 --> 11:31.482
ENGLISH DEPARTMENT, TERM 1, 2026
MIDTERM EXAM

11:40.408 --> 11:42.493
VIEWING IS PROHIBITED
TO UNAUTHORIZED PERSONNEL

11:42.576 --> 11:43.411
Oh, hello.

11:46.247 --> 11:47.415
Must be the exam papers.

11:49.291 --> 11:51.877
Yes, I'm the Head of Academic Affairs,

11:51.961 --> 11:53.629
so I have to check them.

11:55.548 --> 11:57.925
Wow, the exam papers are all here.

11:58.008 --> 12:00.553
When I didn't want to study for exams
back in the day,

12:00.636 --> 12:03.597
I used to daydream about stealing
exam papers with my friends.

12:04.724 --> 12:08.060
Coming up with ways to steal exam papers
was more fun than studying.

12:09.311 --> 12:10.521
I was like that too.

12:11.021 --> 12:12.148
Really?

12:12.648 --> 12:14.567
Mr. Cheon, it's an honor.

12:14.650 --> 12:17.027
Right, you can't be in here.
Let's head out.

12:17.111 --> 12:20.156
It's like we've led parallel lives.

12:21.282 --> 12:26.495
So why did Park Hyeon-ung assault you?

12:28.581 --> 12:29.415
I'm not sure.

12:29.498 --> 12:31.125
Do you have any idea at all?

12:34.128 --> 12:37.506
I created a special class not long ago.

12:37.590 --> 12:39.425
Right. A special class?

12:40.301 --> 12:44.972
But I don't think the class
met Hyeon-ung's expectations.

12:45.473 --> 12:49.226
That's right. This is ten
plus two over two plus… What is it?

12:49.310 --> 12:50.895
We learned this in our first year.

12:50.978 --> 12:52.521
We already covered that last time.

12:52.605 --> 12:55.483
The line segment A10 is seven,
and the triangle ABC…

12:55.566 --> 12:57.193
Why are we only doing reviews?

12:57.276 --> 12:59.111
How will this help us in the exam?

12:59.195 --> 13:00.946
We've been doing this for days.

13:01.781 --> 13:03.157
You should study with us.

13:06.786 --> 13:09.413
The class wasn't made just for Hyeon-ung.

13:09.914 --> 13:12.666
I had to take the other students' levels
into account too.

13:12.750 --> 13:16.587
But it was ultimately for his sake,
wasn't it?

13:17.713 --> 13:18.672
I'm not sure.

13:19.840 --> 13:21.509
Isn't that just our perspective?

13:22.218 --> 13:23.928
DETAILED SCHOOL LIFE RECORD

13:25.137 --> 13:26.180
What about it?

13:26.263 --> 13:29.350
I just can't make any sense of it at all.

13:30.392 --> 13:32.436
You're a top student,
so why did you do it?

13:36.273 --> 13:40.152
A student as smart as you
must know what happens

13:40.236 --> 13:41.946
if you assault a teacher.

13:42.029 --> 13:44.824
What on earth made you angry enough
to ignore all this?

13:48.410 --> 13:52.456
These grades could earn you a scholarship
at one of the top three universities.

13:52.540 --> 13:55.835
You studied your butt off for 12 years
to get into college

13:55.918 --> 13:57.586
and even became the top student.

13:57.670 --> 14:00.214
So why are you acting
like you don't care about all that?

14:01.715 --> 14:04.844
I had bad grades, and even I find it odd.
Do your parents know?

14:15.187 --> 14:16.355
To tell you the truth,

14:16.438 --> 14:19.191
I made a mistake
I shouldn't have as a teacher.

14:19.692 --> 14:23.153
Once a year, the parents come to school
for college counseling,

14:23.237 --> 14:25.823
but Hyeon-ung's parents live far away
and couldn't come.

14:25.906 --> 14:27.241
So I paid them a visit.

14:27.324 --> 14:29.159
HYEON-UNG'S KOREAN BUFFET

14:30.411 --> 14:31.745
They ran a restaurant,

14:32.413 --> 14:36.750
but they seemed so busy that I just ate,
pretending to be a customer.

14:38.711 --> 14:39.545
What?

14:40.129 --> 14:41.589
I guess your parents don't know.

14:44.008 --> 14:46.719
Then I'll have to ask them.

14:48.095 --> 14:49.805
Damn it!

14:53.684 --> 14:56.729
Let go! Let go of me!

14:59.481 --> 15:00.482
Do you feel wronged?

15:01.567 --> 15:02.443
Angry?

15:02.526 --> 15:04.069
I said let go of me!

15:04.570 --> 15:05.529
Let go!

15:05.613 --> 15:07.531
Then ask for help.

15:08.866 --> 15:11.785
The first step in getting help
is to ask for it.

15:17.333 --> 15:21.128
Excuse me, Hyeon-ung.
This month's tuition hasn't been paid yet.

15:22.880 --> 15:23.964
Hey, son!

15:24.048 --> 15:26.300
Your hagwon tuition
hasn't been paid yet, has it?

15:26.383 --> 15:29.094
The restaurant was really busy,
so I forgot.

15:29.178 --> 15:32.681
I'll pay it soon, so no worries.
Just focus on studying hard, son.

15:32.765 --> 15:33.849
You've got this!

15:34.350 --> 15:38.604
After Mr. Cheon visited, the restaurant
was ordered to suspend operations.

15:39.104 --> 15:42.066
They said someone reported it
as an unauthorized building.

15:46.695 --> 15:48.906
Is that why you assaulted your teacher?

15:54.203 --> 15:55.955
Even in these circumstances,

15:57.790 --> 16:01.835
my parents went to a lot of trouble
and found me a private tutor.

16:01.919 --> 16:03.045
Wow.

16:03.128 --> 16:05.130
You did well in the exam.

16:05.214 --> 16:08.300
The exam questions were hard this time.
Do you have a private tutor?

16:09.343 --> 16:10.177
Yes, sir.

16:10.260 --> 16:12.262
Your tutor must be pretty good.

16:12.346 --> 16:13.597
What are they like?

16:14.390 --> 16:16.642
What? You're going to stop tutoring me?

16:16.725 --> 16:19.728
I'm going to stop tutoring
and focus on my graduate studies.

16:21.230 --> 16:25.526
My tutor suddenly quit
right after Mr. Cheon asked about him,

16:26.068 --> 16:27.444
which was odd.

16:35.703 --> 16:38.497
Sir, why are you picking up these stones?

16:38.580 --> 16:40.207
On their way to and from school,

16:40.874 --> 16:43.585
the kids either read books
or watch online lectures.

16:43.669 --> 16:45.504
I can't exactly tell them not to.

16:46.005 --> 16:49.341
I pick them up just in case
they trip on them and get hurt.

16:51.343 --> 16:52.177
Wow.

16:52.761 --> 16:57.349
No wonder people say you should be next
for Seoul Superintendent of Education.

16:57.433 --> 16:59.768
Please don't say things like that.

17:00.436 --> 17:04.440
Anyway, between Minister of Education
and Seoul Superintendent of Education,

17:04.523 --> 17:06.900
which is the higher position?

17:07.609 --> 17:08.444
Pardon?

17:08.527 --> 17:11.822
Well, our Minister of Education
is great in every way.

17:12.322 --> 17:14.616
On the other hand, he's not great at all.

17:15.909 --> 17:18.370
I was just thinking
I might change allegiances.

17:20.080 --> 17:21.915
-I'm being serious.
-My goodness.

17:23.751 --> 17:24.626
By the way,

17:25.252 --> 17:26.545
Inspector Na.

17:27.504 --> 17:29.006
What will happen to Hyeon-ung?

17:30.966 --> 17:32.760
We'll handle it as per protocol.

17:35.471 --> 17:37.264
When I think about Hyeon-ung,

17:37.806 --> 17:40.642
I feel it's right to punish him firmly
for what he did.

17:42.603 --> 17:43.896
But I'm not so sure.

17:43.979 --> 17:47.274
Please leave it to us at the ERPB,
future Superintendent of Education.

17:47.357 --> 17:49.318
Please don't say things like that.

17:49.401 --> 17:51.403
-Not at all.
-Please stop that.

17:51.487 --> 17:54.281
Superintendent of Education,
let me pick up the stones.

17:54.364 --> 17:56.825
-It's fine.
-I'll pick them up for you.

17:56.909 --> 17:59.203
Please give it to me,
Superintendent of Education.

17:59.286 --> 18:01.663
Your Mimiminu channel
is popular with the students.

18:01.747 --> 18:05.584
So I thought my students might like
seeing me on your show.

18:05.667 --> 18:06.668
That's why I came on.

18:06.752 --> 18:09.755
As someone who is true
to their nickname of "true educator,"

18:09.838 --> 18:12.966
the care you have for your students is…

18:13.050 --> 18:14.843
I've met with Hyeon-ung,

18:14.927 --> 18:17.471
and I think you should hear him out.

18:17.554 --> 18:18.889
The chalk snaps!

18:18.972 --> 18:21.141
TEACHER CHEON SANG-YEOL'S ICONIC FINISH!

18:21.225 --> 18:24.770
-I heard this in real life earlier.
-I believe in your potential!

18:24.853 --> 18:29.149
Back in my day,
everyone used to mimic this.

18:30.234 --> 18:33.153
Even the bottom-scoring students
without any foundation…

18:33.237 --> 18:34.988
Looks like you're here to meet a star.

18:35.697 --> 18:37.533
You don't seem like your usual self,

18:37.616 --> 18:40.410
with no interest
in getting to the bottom of this case.

18:41.411 --> 18:44.123
Mr. Cheon seems to matter more to you
than the cause.

18:44.206 --> 18:47.126
Or did the cause never matter to you
in the first place?

18:47.209 --> 18:50.087
We didn't have college entry results
at this level before.

18:50.963 --> 18:52.256
What's your point?

18:58.971 --> 19:00.597
Your perspective is already skewed.

19:02.683 --> 19:05.936
Aren't you thinking
that everything is the student's fault?

19:06.645 --> 19:09.857
Didn't you come here
having already decided who's at fault?

19:09.940 --> 19:12.151
Is what people are saying true?

19:15.237 --> 19:17.948
Are you really blinded
by your personal vendetta?

19:25.873 --> 19:27.082
If that concerns you,

19:28.333 --> 19:30.460
you may quit now.

19:38.051 --> 19:38.886
Hey, Im Han-rim.

19:40.762 --> 19:42.139
Let's do as we always have.

19:58.488 --> 20:00.032
Seriously!

20:05.245 --> 20:06.538
YEAR 3 STUDENT RANKINGS

20:09.124 --> 20:10.918
2ND - CHOI JI-HUN
TEACHER - MR. CHEON

20:12.252 --> 20:14.004
11TH - JUNG SU-JEONG
TEACHER - MR. CHEON

20:17.883 --> 20:20.469
NOAVIS INSTITUTE

20:22.429 --> 20:24.848
NOAVIS INSTITUTE

21:04.304 --> 21:05.305
Who are you?

21:06.181 --> 21:07.599
How did you get in here?

21:07.683 --> 21:11.395
I wanted to register at this institute.

21:11.478 --> 21:12.521
What school are you at?

21:12.604 --> 21:14.690
Chukmyeong Foreign Language High.

21:15.274 --> 21:17.150
I see. Chukmyeong High.

21:17.734 --> 21:18.860
Yes.

21:19.903 --> 21:21.822
Have you heard anything about our hagwon?

21:22.572 --> 21:24.408
That it's a good hagwon.

21:27.327 --> 21:28.370
Sorry.

21:28.453 --> 21:30.998
We're not taking any more students.
Registration is over.

21:31.081 --> 21:33.834
But I had a quick look around,

21:33.917 --> 21:37.462
and the classrooms were all empty, so…

21:37.546 --> 21:39.047
I said registration is over.

21:41.049 --> 21:41.925
Oh, okay.

21:42.634 --> 21:44.219
I'm sorry.

21:53.186 --> 21:54.730
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

21:55.731 --> 21:58.483
-You said you go to Chukmyeong High?
-Yes.

21:58.567 --> 21:59.443
Which class?

21:59.526 --> 22:01.445
Class four in the English Department.

22:01.528 --> 22:04.573
Then you must know Moon Hyeon-o well.
He's the class president.

22:05.157 --> 22:07.951
Yes. Hyeon-o. I know Moon Hyeon-o.

22:08.869 --> 22:10.454
Oh, that's right.

22:11.413 --> 22:14.082
The class four president isn't Hyeon-o.
It's Bo-hyeon.

22:16.001 --> 22:17.794
That's right. It's Bo-hyeon.

22:17.878 --> 22:20.172
I must have confused myself.

22:20.255 --> 22:22.674
-How did you hear about our hagwon?
-What?

22:22.758 --> 22:24.134
Are you even a student?

22:24.217 --> 22:25.552
Of course I am.

22:25.635 --> 22:26.720
-Who are you?
-What?

22:26.803 --> 22:28.930
-Who are you to come--
-Please stop.

22:29.473 --> 22:30.474
Bong Geun-dae.

22:30.557 --> 22:32.225
Hey, Hyeong-ju.

22:32.809 --> 22:35.270
Why did you transfer without telling me?
I was upset.

22:35.354 --> 22:36.480
Where did you move to?

22:36.563 --> 22:38.690
I moved
to Chukmyeong Foreign Language High.

22:39.566 --> 22:41.109
You got a haircut.

22:41.943 --> 22:43.070
How have you been?

22:43.153 --> 22:44.321
Good for you.

22:44.821 --> 22:47.741
I thought a foreign language high school
would suit you better.

22:48.450 --> 22:50.369
-How are things at school?
-It's the same.

22:50.452 --> 22:53.038
They still fight,
and there's still a pecking order.

22:53.872 --> 22:55.624
They don't bully me though.

22:55.707 --> 22:56.833
-Really?
-Yeah.

22:56.917 --> 22:57.751
That's a relief.

22:58.335 --> 23:01.171
How about you? Are you settling in well?

23:06.426 --> 23:07.552
Hey, pull over!

23:07.636 --> 23:08.678
It's Hyeong-ju.

23:08.762 --> 23:09.763
It's Hyeong-ju.

23:11.264 --> 23:12.557
Hey, Kim Hyeong-ju!

23:12.641 --> 23:15.102
We have exams tomorrow.
Why aren't you studying?

23:15.185 --> 23:17.104
Wait, they're having sundae.

23:17.187 --> 23:18.772
-Damn.
-Hi.

23:19.272 --> 23:21.817
-Take your time eating.
-This is so damn good.

23:21.900 --> 23:24.319
Look at him stuff his face.
He's so damn big now.

23:24.403 --> 23:26.696
Studying for exams
made me gain so much weight.

23:26.780 --> 23:29.574
-It's not from studying, you idiot.
-I guess.

23:30.075 --> 23:31.576
Hey.

23:31.660 --> 23:33.745
Is the cheat sheet I told you about ready?

23:33.829 --> 23:35.080
Open up.

23:35.163 --> 23:36.790
You have to share it with me first.

23:36.873 --> 23:38.959
I told you we have different subjects.

23:39.042 --> 23:41.002
I said only the main subjects
are different.

23:41.086 --> 23:42.337
Eat this.

23:43.630 --> 23:44.923
Fuck. Seriously.

23:45.006 --> 23:46.466
Hey, whoa!

23:47.134 --> 23:49.010
Play rock, paper, scissors for it.

23:49.094 --> 23:50.554
Okay.

23:50.637 --> 23:52.222
-Rock, paper, scissors.
-Scissors.

23:52.305 --> 23:53.473
Rock, paper, scissors!

23:53.557 --> 23:54.724
You fucker.

23:56.143 --> 23:58.478
Okay, last one.

23:58.979 --> 24:00.147
Rock, paper, scissors.

24:00.647 --> 24:02.190
-I get it first.
-Hey.

24:24.504 --> 24:26.339
REPORT ON CHUKMYEONG HIGH

24:28.383 --> 24:30.260
BY BONG GEUN-DAE, ERPB

25:04.085 --> 25:05.212
Hey! Damn it.

25:05.921 --> 25:07.631
Hey, you fucking bitch!

25:07.714 --> 25:09.591
That crazy bitch.

25:10.383 --> 25:11.593
Where are you going?

25:13.345 --> 25:15.430
Fucking hell. Seriously, stop!

25:15.931 --> 25:17.224
-Stop right there!
-Fuck!

25:17.307 --> 25:18.808
Seriously. Damn it.

25:22.270 --> 25:23.438
Are you done running?

25:23.522 --> 25:25.315
Fucking hell, crazy bitch.

25:26.733 --> 25:28.944
-You fucking nutcase.
-Are you done running?

25:31.655 --> 25:33.532
That must hurt.

25:33.615 --> 25:34.824
It does, doesn't it?

25:34.908 --> 25:38.286
My heart almost exploded,
you fucking bitch.

25:40.413 --> 25:41.248
Han-rim.

25:41.873 --> 25:44.125
How many more beatings
until you get it together?

25:46.253 --> 25:47.295
Are you Joan of Arc?

25:47.796 --> 25:49.798
Why the hell would you butt in,

25:49.881 --> 25:53.051
trying to help an outcast
when you're just a loser yourself?

25:53.677 --> 25:56.096
You sure stick your nose in
when you ain't got shit.

25:56.846 --> 25:59.182
Rip her mouth open for me too.

25:59.266 --> 26:01.643
Should I? All right, Han-rim.

26:03.436 --> 26:05.981
Come here. I missed your lips.

26:06.481 --> 26:07.941
Hey, what are you guys doing?

26:18.034 --> 26:18.868
Just a grunt.

26:19.452 --> 26:21.830
Mind your own business and be on your way.

26:21.913 --> 26:23.081
Just be on your way

26:23.707 --> 26:25.542
and "salute" for your country.

26:26.793 --> 26:29.921
I'm a bit busy with my friends right now.

26:30.880 --> 26:31.756
Is that true?

26:33.341 --> 26:34.426
Yes, it is.

26:35.135 --> 26:36.136
"Friends."

26:37.304 --> 26:38.680
Whoa.

26:40.265 --> 26:41.600
-The weather…
-You scared?

26:41.683 --> 26:43.435
-The weather's weird.
-He got scared.

26:43.518 --> 26:45.353
Scared, my ass.

26:45.437 --> 26:46.980
-Are you scared?
-I'm not.

26:47.063 --> 26:48.523
You moron.

26:48.607 --> 26:49.691
Should I help you?

26:53.320 --> 26:54.904
Ask for my help.

26:57.157 --> 26:59.951
The first step in getting help
is to ask for it.

27:05.540 --> 27:07.667
Who is this man? Is he your boyfriend?

27:09.669 --> 27:11.254
Disgusting.

27:22.057 --> 27:23.892
That's so cool.

27:24.392 --> 27:26.519
-He's going.
-Hey, he's leaving.

27:36.112 --> 27:36.946
Please…

27:38.114 --> 27:39.991
Please help me. Please?

27:44.412 --> 27:45.413
I heard you.

27:55.965 --> 27:57.550
What are you going to do?

27:58.218 --> 28:00.720
What? Is a grunt going to hit a civilian?

28:02.180 --> 28:03.390
Yes, I am.

28:04.015 --> 28:05.141
Damn it.

28:09.896 --> 28:11.564
-Let's go, you crazy bitch!
-Damn it!

28:11.648 --> 28:13.316
-Fuck.
-Fuck, take me with you.

28:13.400 --> 28:14.401
Son of a bitch.

28:14.484 --> 28:16.069
Shit, this fucking hurts.

28:27.122 --> 28:28.123
Well done.

28:59.487 --> 29:00.572
-Thanks for this.
-Sure.

29:07.036 --> 29:08.872
All right, let's see.

29:09.956 --> 29:14.294
It's fascinating that the students
ranked 1 to 11 in the grade

29:14.377 --> 29:15.879
are all in your class.

29:15.962 --> 29:20.049
I'm sure you've already discovered
they all come from prominent families.

29:20.133 --> 29:23.928
The other teachers felt a lot of pressure,
so I took them on myself.

29:24.012 --> 29:26.473
-Just as I expected. I believe in you.
-Gosh.

29:26.556 --> 29:27.640
It was nothing.

29:28.433 --> 29:30.935
But they all seem to go to this hagwon.

29:31.019 --> 29:33.229
A hagwon called Noavis Institute.

29:33.813 --> 29:35.815
All the kids but Park Hyeon-ung.

29:35.899 --> 29:37.692
Are you familiar with this hagwon?

29:39.736 --> 29:43.782
I have heard a rumor that they offer
elite courses for a select few.

29:44.616 --> 29:47.911
The hagwon must be in a tight spot.

29:47.994 --> 29:49.704
They push their students so hard,

29:49.788 --> 29:53.625
yet the top student is Park Hyeon-ung,
who doesn't even go to a hagwon.

29:54.209 --> 29:55.835
I heard that hagwons these days

29:55.919 --> 30:00.089
are going all out to get the top students
for marketing purposes.

30:01.007 --> 30:02.425
I heard about that too.

30:04.469 --> 30:06.346
Okay, here's the thing.

30:07.889 --> 30:11.392
Let's say Hyeon-ung can't take the exam
because of the recent assault.

30:11.893 --> 30:14.312
Then who would benefit the most from this?

30:15.230 --> 30:17.315
Is it Noavis Institute
that's in a tight spot?

30:17.398 --> 30:19.818
Is it the kids
who would each move up one rank?

30:20.318 --> 30:21.361
Or…

30:22.320 --> 30:25.573
Is it Jung Su-jeong
who would move up not only in rank

30:26.199 --> 30:27.659
but also in tier?

30:31.621 --> 30:34.499
What are you trying to say right now?

30:40.255 --> 30:43.716
Mr. Cheon, do you know
a student called Han Ye-ri?

30:44.676 --> 30:45.510
I'm not sure.

30:45.593 --> 30:49.597
We were at Soyeon Girls' High School
before here.

30:50.098 --> 30:51.891
She goes there. Don't you know her?

30:55.144 --> 30:57.355
You were her middle school
homeroom teacher.

31:01.067 --> 31:02.610
Her name does ring a bell.

31:02.694 --> 31:03.653
Okay.

31:03.736 --> 31:05.947
Ye-ri did well academically

31:06.030 --> 31:09.534
and had been preparing to enroll here
at Chukmyeong Foreign Language High.

31:10.034 --> 31:13.288
But she never made it
because she missed her final exam.

31:13.371 --> 31:14.372
Is that so?

31:14.455 --> 31:15.582
Yes.

31:15.665 --> 31:19.002
And the student who was able
to come here in her place

31:19.085 --> 31:22.755
was Jung Su-jeong,
the student in your class.

31:23.256 --> 31:24.090
Isn't that right?

31:27.635 --> 31:29.804
Ye-ri had been doing so well in school,

31:30.346 --> 31:32.807
so why did she miss her exam?

31:32.891 --> 31:35.727
Was it because her parents
weren't as privileged as Su-jeong's?

31:39.898 --> 31:44.235
Is that why you created a class
that cut into her study time,

31:44.319 --> 31:46.029
stole her tutor, and pulled strings

31:46.112 --> 31:50.033
to sabotage her parents' store,
pushing her to violence, like Hyeon-ung?

31:50.950 --> 31:53.328
So she would mentally break down
and miss the exam?

32:03.212 --> 32:06.549
What? Do you still have
unfinished business with me?

32:07.050 --> 32:09.302
What do I need to do to end this?

32:09.802 --> 32:10.762
What?

32:14.432 --> 32:16.184
You just need to tell me one thing.

32:17.185 --> 32:18.353
Cheon Sang-yeol.

32:25.902 --> 32:28.446
What Cheon Sang-yeol did to you.

32:30.281 --> 32:31.449
Just tell me that.

32:43.086 --> 32:46.172
You think ranking first in your grade
makes you tier one, don't you?

32:46.839 --> 32:49.884
Each person has a tier
that suits them best.

32:49.968 --> 32:53.388
In your case,
it would be around tier nine.

32:54.263 --> 32:55.890
Your parents are no different.

32:55.974 --> 32:57.767
In fact, your whole family is

32:58.559 --> 32:59.560
tier nine.

33:04.148 --> 33:05.650
Son of a bitch.

33:06.567 --> 33:07.860
Son of a bitch.

33:20.081 --> 33:22.208
She caused a serious problem.

33:22.291 --> 33:24.502
Did you come all the way here
just on her word?

33:28.673 --> 33:32.927
I never said Han Ye-ri
was a problem student.

33:33.511 --> 33:36.180
You barely remembered her a moment ago.

33:37.098 --> 33:40.810
Yet you're well aware of the issues
she caused at Soyeon Girls' High School.

33:40.893 --> 33:43.730
The fact that the ERPB was there
means there was an issue.

33:44.772 --> 33:45.606
But…

33:48.109 --> 33:49.819
what are you playing at here?

33:50.653 --> 33:51.779
I think that's enough.

33:52.822 --> 33:54.323
You know Hyeon-ung…

33:55.783 --> 33:59.162
Park Hyeon-ung,
whom you are so concerned about…

34:01.873 --> 34:04.000
He will definitely take
the upcoming exams.

34:07.086 --> 34:08.463
Will he?

34:12.717 --> 34:13.843
Thank you.

34:17.889 --> 34:18.723
I believe

34:19.515 --> 34:21.267
in the potential of the ERPB.

34:39.702 --> 34:41.704
-Don't you think it's a bit much?
-Yeah.

34:42.955 --> 34:44.082
-It's Hyeon-ung.
-What?

34:44.165 --> 34:45.333
What is he doing here?

34:46.334 --> 34:47.210
What the hell?

34:50.546 --> 34:52.590
How could he even think about showing up?

34:52.673 --> 34:54.008
I know, right?

34:54.092 --> 34:56.260
Wow, so brazen.

34:56.761 --> 34:58.721
If it were me, I'd never come in.

35:20.827 --> 35:22.620
What on earth are you doing?

35:22.703 --> 35:25.373
How come Park Hyeon-ung
is able to take the exams?

35:25.873 --> 35:29.085
For messing up her mock exams,

35:29.168 --> 35:32.255
Su-jeong must now get tier-one marks
in all subjects in the midterms.

35:32.338 --> 35:34.340
I already told you this.

35:35.133 --> 35:36.134
Please have your tea.

35:36.217 --> 35:39.470
If this is how it is, I can't promise you
Superintendent of Education.

35:40.596 --> 35:44.100
Why can't Su-jeong get into tier one
when the others manage to?

35:44.183 --> 35:47.520
I pay you considerably more
than the others do. Is it not enough?

35:47.603 --> 35:48.896
For crying out loud!

35:49.605 --> 35:51.732
It's not my fault
your daughter is a brickhead.

35:52.316 --> 35:53.151
Excuse me?

35:53.234 --> 35:55.486
The others all do it,
so what is it with Su-jeong?

35:55.570 --> 35:58.406
Why set the table
if she can't handle a spoon?

35:59.157 --> 36:00.324
Why are you so brazen?

36:00.408 --> 36:03.995
The Superintendent of Education role?
I can get it without your help.

36:04.078 --> 36:06.622
It's you who has a lot to lose, not me.

36:06.706 --> 36:08.791
Can Su-jeong get into college without me?

36:10.459 --> 36:13.754
So just stay out of it, okay?

36:13.838 --> 36:15.548
I'll handle everything.

36:16.048 --> 36:18.134
And we're in a café. Mind your manners.

36:32.064 --> 36:33.441
Oh, you gave me a fright.

36:35.902 --> 36:37.820
-What are these?
-Hold them up.

36:37.904 --> 36:38.821
What?

36:42.450 --> 36:44.994
Didn't you get over it all
when you ran around the track?

36:45.077 --> 36:45.953
No, I didn't.

36:49.874 --> 36:52.919
It's now past six o'clock,
and I need to add RAM to my computer…

36:56.047 --> 36:57.924
What on earth is the matter with you?

36:58.007 --> 36:59.133
Damn it.

36:59.217 --> 37:00.968
It's Inspector Na Hwa-jin.

37:01.636 --> 37:05.223
-I don't think I recognize him anymore.
-What?

37:05.306 --> 37:08.017
He won't even try
to hear Park Hyeon-ung out!

37:08.517 --> 37:11.437
And he only sides with Mr. Cheon.
For God's sake.

37:11.520 --> 37:13.105
That personal vendetta thing…

37:13.189 --> 37:14.941
It's not like that at all.

37:16.901 --> 37:17.735
Then what is it?

37:17.818 --> 37:19.779
Ever since visiting Han Ye-ri,

37:19.862 --> 37:23.824
Inspector Na Hwa-jin
has been keeping an eye on Mr. Cheon.

37:23.908 --> 37:27.870
He told me to keep looking
into Mr. Cheon's students.

37:27.954 --> 37:32.041
That's why I looked into Noavis Institute
and paid them a visit.

37:32.541 --> 37:33.376
Really?

37:33.459 --> 37:34.502
Yes.

37:35.211 --> 37:37.463
Then why was I the only one
who didn't know?

37:38.381 --> 37:39.340
Why?

37:39.423 --> 37:40.466
Well…

37:41.217 --> 37:44.470
He said you're not very good
at deceiving other people

37:44.553 --> 37:48.015
and that you're a terrible liar.

37:49.725 --> 37:51.060
Damn it.

37:51.852 --> 37:52.687
Gosh.

37:53.604 --> 37:54.605
Whoa.

38:05.783 --> 38:06.617
Deputy Bong.

38:08.369 --> 38:09.704
What's gotten into her?

38:10.913 --> 38:14.750
She says she's acting like this
because she feels guilty.

38:18.212 --> 38:20.589
You call that fast?

38:37.898 --> 38:39.358
Why did you do it?

38:40.609 --> 38:43.362
Why did you pretend
you weren't suspicious of Mr. Cheon?

38:44.947 --> 38:46.991
I didn't pretend.

38:48.367 --> 38:49.744
I hoped otherwise.

38:52.663 --> 38:55.791
I hoped there would be
at least one teacher like that.

39:00.171 --> 39:01.672
I should've known better.

39:02.381 --> 39:04.842
Why didn't you say anything?

39:04.925 --> 39:07.136
I think you could've told me.
Me, of all people.

39:07.219 --> 39:09.430
No, I think you should've told me.

39:09.930 --> 39:12.475
I doubted your intention.

39:12.975 --> 39:15.811
You made me doubt you!

39:21.734 --> 39:22.568
Han-rim.

39:24.278 --> 39:25.112
Yes, sir!

39:25.696 --> 39:27.031
We aren't strangers.

39:30.910 --> 39:32.411
Let's do as we always have.

39:36.832 --> 39:37.666
All right?

39:39.668 --> 39:41.420
Understood, sir!

39:41.921 --> 39:44.715
-That bastard Cheon Sang-yeol did this.
-Damn it.

39:46.926 --> 39:49.887
He's not the type to sit around.
We'll have much more to do.

39:51.889 --> 39:54.266
Where are you going?
I said we'll have more to do.

39:55.393 --> 39:56.227
I was just…

39:56.310 --> 39:57.728
Come here. Just stay here.

39:57.812 --> 39:58.979
Mr. Na Hwa-jin?

40:04.026 --> 40:05.319
We're from the police.

40:05.403 --> 40:08.364
We received reports
that you harmed innocent students

40:08.447 --> 40:11.367
during your time as inspector
at Daehan High and Guun High.

40:15.663 --> 40:18.958
We are enforcing search and seizure
of the ERPB for abuse of power

40:19.041 --> 40:20.918
and violations of recruitment laws.

40:23.838 --> 40:27.258
Following a large-scale search and seizure
of the ERPB,

40:27.341 --> 40:29.552
amid a personal revenge scandal,

40:29.635 --> 40:34.056
the prosecution is investigating
Minister Choi on charges of tax evasion.

40:34.140 --> 40:36.350
They said they would protect
educational rights,

40:36.434 --> 40:39.437
so I had no idea
they would attack our teachers like this.

40:39.520 --> 40:41.939
Especially not someone like Mr. Cheon.

40:42.022 --> 40:45.776
How do you see the ERPB's investigation
into teacher Cheon Sang-yeol?

40:45.860 --> 40:48.404
It feels like the ERPB jumped the gun.

40:48.487 --> 40:50.072
After it was revealed

40:50.156 --> 40:53.117
that the ERPB was borne out
of a personal vendetta

40:53.200 --> 40:56.328
by the victim's father and fiancé
over a two-year-old case,

40:56.412 --> 40:58.289
it seems they tried to muddy the waters

40:58.372 --> 41:01.125
by shifting their targets
from students to teachers.

41:01.208 --> 41:04.795
They likely targeted a well-known figure
like Cheon Sang-yeol

41:04.879 --> 41:06.422
for similar reasons.

41:08.466 --> 41:11.594
It looks like Choi Gang-seok
has screwed up big time.

41:11.677 --> 41:13.262
Should we run some articles?

41:14.305 --> 41:18.225
How about we corner the ERPB
and push to impeach the president?

41:18.309 --> 41:22.354
"We were duped by Minister Choi
when he first proposed the ERPB bill."

41:24.607 --> 41:26.567
Perfect time to shift the blame, isn't it?

41:36.368 --> 41:38.621
Announce we'll hold
a Board of Education meeting.

41:40.414 --> 41:41.957
In the hiring of the inspector,

41:42.041 --> 41:44.793
there was abuse of power
by the Minister of Education.

41:45.294 --> 41:46.712
Do you admit it?

41:57.765 --> 42:00.559
It all played out exactly as you expected.

42:00.643 --> 42:02.520
Impressive connections, don't you think?

42:02.603 --> 42:05.231
The fact that the prosecution,
the police, the press,

42:05.314 --> 42:07.816
and even the tax office
all operated as one is just…

42:07.900 --> 42:10.152
I bet even the president can't match that.

42:10.236 --> 42:12.530
Is this the time to be impressed?

42:12.613 --> 42:13.948
Shouldn't we do something?

42:14.865 --> 42:17.535
We have to stay locked up here
until next week anyway.

42:17.618 --> 42:18.827
Next week? Why?

42:21.163 --> 42:23.666
Chukmyeong High's exams are next week.

42:24.416 --> 42:26.919
They won't let us do anything before then.

42:27.002 --> 42:28.254
Goddamn it.

42:28.796 --> 42:30.798
S sub n equals n squared times a sub n.

42:30.881 --> 42:33.259
Something should come to mind
when you see this.

42:38.013 --> 42:40.266
Right, focus on me.

42:40.349 --> 42:44.436
Okay, here it's n plus one squared
times a sub n plus one…

42:44.937 --> 42:45.854
You're here.

42:45.938 --> 42:47.106
Please take a seat.

42:53.362 --> 42:55.864
I saw you took care of the ERPB
all on your own.

42:55.948 --> 42:57.408
All I have are my connections.

42:58.325 --> 43:01.328
-You were a great help too.
-It was nothing.

43:02.329 --> 43:04.373
Enough about the ERPB.

43:05.332 --> 43:06.458
What about Su-jeong?

43:09.128 --> 43:11.005
Right, ma'am.

43:24.351 --> 43:25.728
What is this?

43:25.811 --> 43:27.730
Tell Su-jeong to memorize it all.

43:27.813 --> 43:30.733
Since she can't handle a spoon,
we should spoon-feed her.

43:32.401 --> 43:34.236
You didn't show the other kids, right?

43:36.030 --> 43:39.366
Please take care of my fundraiser
for the Superintendent of Education.

43:39.450 --> 43:40.909
Don't worry.

43:41.410 --> 43:45.080
We will donate enough
to have your funding overflowing.

43:45.706 --> 43:48.751
If this exam goes well,
you'll be the Superintendent of Education.

43:49.793 --> 43:50.794
My gosh.

43:54.590 --> 43:56.675
When I'm told to provide backup support,

43:56.759 --> 44:02.556
I send necessary materials
to the inspectors and look things up…

44:02.640 --> 44:04.808
You won't get anything
from questioning him.

44:06.018 --> 44:09.188
He's just a public official
who does what his superiors tell him.

44:11.398 --> 44:13.275
Don't waste your energy and let him go.

44:16.820 --> 44:18.864
-Deputy Bong.
-Hey.

44:19.865 --> 44:22.660
They said I'm free to go now.

44:23.577 --> 44:24.870
Bring that thing to me.

44:27.206 --> 44:28.624
Pardon? Bring what…

44:28.707 --> 44:30.709
The assignment transfer application.

44:31.293 --> 44:33.420
I'll sign it off for you,
so bring it to me.

44:34.004 --> 44:34.880
You wanted it.

44:35.881 --> 44:39.843
I thought about it again,
and I've changed my mind a little.

44:39.927 --> 44:41.178
Just bring it, you brat.

44:41.261 --> 44:43.055
But I really thought about it again--

44:43.138 --> 44:44.473
Just bring it to me!

44:51.063 --> 44:51.897
Yes, sir.

44:53.440 --> 44:55.150
-Assignment transfer?
-No, but…

44:55.234 --> 44:56.485
-I really--
-Hurry up!

44:56.568 --> 44:58.445
Yes, sir. I'll go and get it.

45:00.614 --> 45:01.990
I AM REQUESTING A TRANSFER OF…

45:06.120 --> 45:08.080
Please just take a look.

45:08.914 --> 45:09.748
Wait…

45:18.257 --> 45:21.927
The way things are now,
staying at the ERPB won't do you any good.

45:22.010 --> 45:23.470
Inspector Na Hwa-jin,

45:24.179 --> 45:25.264
you sign it too.

45:28.434 --> 45:31.437
I won't think of it as you whining,
so stand tall.

45:32.855 --> 45:33.897
Keep your chin up.

45:49.496 --> 45:50.706
Goodbye.

46:01.091 --> 46:03.010
Oops, sorry.

46:06.013 --> 46:07.598
What? Get back to studying.

46:08.182 --> 46:09.767
Quick, pick it up. It's in the way.

46:12.144 --> 46:13.812
You'll make him cry.

46:20.611 --> 46:22.112
Good morning.

46:23.947 --> 46:26.283
Put your textbooks away,
and shut the other door.

46:41.048 --> 46:42.341
Good luck on the exam.

47:14.873 --> 47:15.958
Take care, sir.

47:16.041 --> 47:17.918
-Goodbye, sir.
-You did well.

47:18.001 --> 47:21.255
What was your real motive
for establishing the ERPB?

47:22.840 --> 47:24.508
Do you seek to avenge your daughter?

47:25.717 --> 47:28.762
Or are you trying
to use your dead daughter

47:28.846 --> 47:30.013
for political gain?

47:30.848 --> 47:33.684
Why did you target the teacher
Cheon Sang-yeol?

47:33.767 --> 47:36.436
As the public turned against you
over revenge allegations,

47:36.520 --> 47:37.646
weren't you deflecting?

47:42.860 --> 47:44.903
EXAM MANAGEMENT OFFICE
RESTRICTED AREA

47:49.783 --> 47:51.702
EXAM MARKING PROGRAM
SELECT TOPIC: CALCULUS

47:51.785 --> 47:53.245
Can you pass that to me?

47:57.457 --> 47:59.293
JUNG SU-JEONG
SUBJECT: CALCULUS

47:59.376 --> 48:00.419
It's correct.

48:05.299 --> 48:06.758
JUNG SU-JEONG, SCORE: 0

48:09.636 --> 48:11.889
Pass me the math exam paper.

48:13.140 --> 48:13.974
Here.

48:17.895 --> 48:19.730
-Pass me the English exam paper.
-Here.

48:23.400 --> 48:25.277
What? What's going on?

48:35.829 --> 48:37.039
Stop the exam immediately.

48:37.122 --> 48:39.082
-What do you mean?
-Stop right now.

48:39.166 --> 48:42.419
Those at the back! Collect all exam papers
and answer sheets. Now!

48:43.003 --> 48:44.880
-The exam isn't over yet, sir.
-This is…

48:44.963 --> 48:47.507
What are you waiting for? Do it now!

48:48.091 --> 48:49.301
The exam paper is…

48:49.384 --> 48:50.636
Wait!

48:53.388 --> 48:54.222
What?

48:55.390 --> 48:56.683
The exam isn't over yet.

48:56.767 --> 48:57.935
Damn it.

48:58.477 --> 49:01.063
-Collect them right now!
-Stop right there.

49:01.730 --> 49:03.899
Guys, sit down.
You have to take your exam.

49:05.817 --> 49:07.945
That's right. Good.

49:08.028 --> 49:10.530
You were so worried
the kids might get distracted.

49:10.614 --> 49:13.617
Is there a particular reason
they shouldn't take their exams?

49:15.661 --> 49:17.037
They're the wrong exam papers.

49:17.120 --> 49:19.957
We'll find out what happened,
void all exams, and retake them.

49:20.040 --> 49:21.583
No. There will be no retakes.

49:21.667 --> 49:23.251
Someone switched the exam…

49:28.465 --> 49:30.717
The ERPB replaced the exam papers.

49:31.593 --> 49:32.427
How…

49:32.928 --> 49:34.846
-How did the ERPB…
-I know, right?

49:34.930 --> 49:39.142
We were all locked up at
the police station, so how did we do it?

49:40.060 --> 49:41.395
Inspector Na Hwa-jin,

49:42.145 --> 49:43.271
you sign it too.

49:49.027 --> 49:51.488
MINISTER OF EDUCATION
REPLACE THE EXAM PAPERS

49:55.617 --> 49:57.285
TEAM LEADER

49:57.369 --> 49:59.246
CHEON SANG-YEOL SON OF A BITCH

50:04.376 --> 50:05.544
CHUKMYEONG HIGH GUIDE.PDF

50:05.627 --> 50:08.171
PS I'M STEALING THEM.
MY HIGH SCHOOL DREAMS HAVE COME TRUE

50:37.909 --> 50:40.537
It's clear you tampered with the exam,
so it stops now.

50:41.121 --> 50:43.248
Give that here. Stop it. Stop working.

50:43.331 --> 50:45.167
Stop working, you punk!

50:45.250 --> 50:46.126
Let go!

50:47.210 --> 50:48.128
Let go!

50:49.337 --> 50:50.505
Let go, you jerk!

50:54.092 --> 50:55.010
Mr. Cheon!

50:56.303 --> 50:59.306
You must not cause a disturbance
or be disruptive during exams,

50:59.389 --> 51:00.807
even if you are a teacher.

51:02.267 --> 51:03.101
Damn it.

51:07.022 --> 51:08.148
Damn you, ERPB!

51:10.150 --> 51:11.068
Mr. Cheon!

51:11.151 --> 51:13.236
You damn bastard!

51:26.124 --> 51:28.502
ERPB SPECIAL PROJECT

51:28.585 --> 51:31.463
Mic test. One, two.

51:32.005 --> 51:35.008
Hello, this is
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau.

51:35.092 --> 51:39.554
Please stop your exam for a moment
and look at the screen.

51:39.638 --> 51:43.266
A special video will start shortly.

51:43.350 --> 51:44.434
Title.

51:45.310 --> 51:48.772
The Reason the ERPB
Replaced the Exam Papers.

51:48.855 --> 51:51.775
The reason.

51:54.778 --> 51:58.365
THE REASON THE ERPB
REPLACED THE EXAM PAPERS

51:58.448 --> 52:00.742
On Mr. Cheon's original exam paper,

52:00.826 --> 52:04.162
the answer to question one
was "one over two."

52:04.246 --> 52:06.498
Being multiple choice,
the answer was number one.

52:06.581 --> 52:08.125
What about Jung Su-jeong?

52:09.417 --> 52:11.419
Jung Su-jeong's answer to question one is…

52:16.007 --> 52:16.842
number one too.

52:17.425 --> 52:20.053
And the answer
to written-response question one

52:20.137 --> 52:21.555
was "three cosine theta

52:21.638 --> 52:25.433
equals four cosine cubed theta
minus three cosine theta."

52:25.517 --> 52:27.227
What about Jung Su-jeong?

52:28.895 --> 52:31.064
Jung Su-jeong's answer is…

52:36.236 --> 52:37.654
also "cosine three theta

52:37.737 --> 52:42.742
equals four cosine cubed theta
minus three cosine theta."

52:42.826 --> 52:47.455
Today, Jung Su-jeong took the exam
with the exam papers replaced by the ERPB.

52:47.539 --> 52:48.665
Her math score is

52:49.249 --> 52:50.333
zero.

52:52.127 --> 52:53.420
But the thing is…

52:53.503 --> 52:59.342
If you compare the math exam paper
Mr. Cheon had originally set

52:59.426 --> 53:03.180
with Jung Su-jeong's answer card,

53:03.930 --> 53:05.182
the score would be 100.

53:05.807 --> 53:08.935
The exam questions were actually the same.

53:09.019 --> 53:12.856
Only the order of the questions
had changed.

53:13.356 --> 53:17.736
A top student who has always ranked 11th
in her year got a zero.

53:18.236 --> 53:20.655
She may not have felt well today,

53:20.739 --> 53:23.491
or she may have misaligned her answers
by one row.

53:23.575 --> 53:26.536
Even so, it's too much of a coincidence

53:27.120 --> 53:31.458
that all her answers match
the order of the questions

53:31.541 --> 53:34.127
on the exam paper
Mr. Cheon had originally set.

53:35.253 --> 53:36.254
That's right.

53:49.851 --> 53:52.812
Destroying evidence
is a serious criminal offense!

53:53.647 --> 53:55.732
-Were the answers on her hands?
-Is she crazy?

53:57.234 --> 53:58.068
What is this?

53:58.652 --> 54:00.779
Tell Su-jeong to memorize it all.

54:00.862 --> 54:03.782
Since she can't handle a spoon,
we should spoon-feed her.

54:05.242 --> 54:06.076
You didn't show…

54:07.702 --> 54:08.995
No. This is nothing.

54:10.121 --> 54:11.039
Guys, it's nothing.

54:12.040 --> 54:14.125
Tell Su-jeong to memorize it all.

54:14.626 --> 54:16.920
You didn't show the other kids, right?

54:17.003 --> 54:20.590
Please take care of my fundraiser
for the Superintendent of Education.

54:20.674 --> 54:25.762
Don't worry. We will donate enough
to have your funding overflowing.

54:27.013 --> 54:30.350
If this exam goes well,
you'll be the Superintendent of Education.

54:31.476 --> 54:32.519
My gosh.

54:37.357 --> 54:39.401
Guys, it's really nothing!

54:39.484 --> 54:41.403
Mr. Cheon, is this real?

54:41.486 --> 54:42.696
Don't you trust me?

54:42.779 --> 54:45.031
-How could you?
-Everyone, sit down. Okay?

54:45.115 --> 54:46.324
I'll explain. No!

54:47.200 --> 54:49.160
-Da-yeon.
-We studied so damn hard!

54:49.244 --> 54:51.079
We have to go to SNU together, Da-yeon.

54:51.162 --> 54:52.956
Don't you trust me? Seriously?

54:56.293 --> 54:59.212
Will that give you enough energy to study?
Here, have more.

55:01.798 --> 55:02.882
You've turned out well.

55:04.134 --> 55:05.719
Just keep growing like that.

55:06.803 --> 55:09.347
Let me deal
with trash like Cheon Sang-yeol.

55:09.431 --> 55:11.016
I'll kick his butt.

55:13.768 --> 55:16.062
Thanks for the food. I'm off.

55:17.731 --> 55:19.482
Don't stay out too late.

55:23.361 --> 55:24.237
You believe that?

55:24.321 --> 55:26.239
-No, guys.
-Did you tell her?

55:26.323 --> 55:28.116
-I didn't.
-Did you really tell her?

55:28.199 --> 55:29.492
Guys, I really didn't!

55:30.327 --> 55:32.704
I'm Hwang Gi-tae,
the Mirae Daehan Party leader.

55:32.787 --> 55:35.582
As I mentioned
in the last press conference,

55:35.665 --> 55:39.836
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau
was created out of personal vendetta.

55:39.919 --> 55:42.213
But there is a bigger problem.

55:42.297 --> 55:44.674
They cannot be controlled,
no matter what they do,

55:44.758 --> 55:47.177
if they operate under the pretext
of ERPB activity,

55:48.053 --> 55:51.222
simply due to the extralegal Article 8
of the Establishment Act.

55:51.723 --> 55:55.977
"All acts by an inspector
during on-site guidance and investigations

55:56.061 --> 55:59.773
are not subject
to legal and institutional restrictions."

55:59.856 --> 56:04.069
Even if the inspector committed murder,
it would not be in violation of the law.

56:06.154 --> 56:08.740
Right now, you may be satisfied
with their actions.

56:08.823 --> 56:12.285
But in the future,
an irreparable tragedy is bound to occur.

56:12.369 --> 56:14.454
-Watch your mouth.
-Quiet down over there.

56:14.537 --> 56:16.748
-Stop talking nonsense.
-You know we're right!

56:17.832 --> 56:20.293
-Please be quiet.
-Minister of Education.

56:20.960 --> 56:23.129
Do you remember the trial two years ago?

56:24.672 --> 56:27.717
I have met someone
who clearly remembers that day.

56:29.427 --> 56:31.805
Is the prison guard,
Mr. Yoon Sun-yeol, present?

56:32.764 --> 56:34.349
-Yes, sir.
-Please come forward.

56:39.813 --> 56:43.108
Would you tell us what you witnessed
that day as it happened?

56:44.442 --> 56:49.030
As we escorted the accused, Cho Gyu-cheol,
to the transport vehicle after the trial,

56:49.531 --> 56:52.534
a man drove his car at him.

57:00.333 --> 57:03.586
Is this the man you are talking about?

57:04.629 --> 57:06.464
Yes, that's correct.

57:08.508 --> 57:10.343
Although it remained as an attempt,

57:10.427 --> 57:13.680
the inspector was so enraged
that he tried to commit murder.

57:13.763 --> 57:17.600
And the Minister of Education appointed
this person as the ERPB inspector.

57:17.684 --> 57:20.770
Do these people really have any right
to discuss education?

57:20.854 --> 57:23.440
The ERPB must be abolished at all costs.

57:25.150 --> 57:27.694
Mr. Yoon, you may return to your seat.

57:28.319 --> 57:31.156
Minister Choi,
you may make your counterarguments.

57:35.452 --> 57:36.703
Well…

57:37.203 --> 57:38.621
Before I proceed,

57:38.705 --> 57:41.624
I believe
there's a far more important issue

57:42.876 --> 57:45.336
that needs to be addressed first.

57:45.420 --> 57:49.090
Mr. Chairperson, please restrict
the discussion to relevant issues!

57:50.175 --> 57:51.217
Please restrict it!

57:51.301 --> 57:54.429
Please be quiet.
I will proceed as I see fit.

57:55.597 --> 57:59.851
Not long ago, the ERPB conducted
a full-scale investigation

57:59.934 --> 58:02.645
into Chukmyeong Foreign Language High.

58:03.855 --> 58:04.898
As a result,

58:05.607 --> 58:07.734
we uncovered evidence of collusion

58:07.817 --> 58:11.446
among Cheon Sang-yeol, the parents,
and Noavis Institute

58:12.030 --> 58:14.199
to manipulate the grades.

58:15.492 --> 58:18.453
Cheon Sang-yeol
not only leaked exam questions

58:18.536 --> 58:20.872
through Noavis Institute in advance,

58:20.955 --> 58:25.126
but he even leaked the exam papers
for the recent midterms.

58:25.210 --> 58:26.586
No way…

58:27.587 --> 58:29.130
Now I will disclose

58:30.256 --> 58:33.384
the names of parents involved
with Cheon Sang-yeol

58:33.468 --> 58:35.428
in the manipulation of grades.

58:40.266 --> 58:43.853
PH Group Chairman's wife, Kim Yeong-ran.

58:43.937 --> 58:44.979
Oh my God!

58:45.480 --> 58:47.732
Daehan Media owner, Choi Pil-geun.

58:47.815 --> 58:50.068
Former NTS Commissioner, Joo Hyeon-ju.

58:50.151 --> 58:53.321
Former Chief Prosecutor
of Seoul Western District, Kim Jin-cheol.

58:53.821 --> 58:56.157
Doil Semiconductors CEO, Lee Jin-bong.

58:56.241 --> 58:58.743
Former Minister of Environment,
Kim Hui-jin.

58:58.826 --> 59:01.454
Researcher at Seo Bio, Ma Seong-hun.

59:01.538 --> 59:03.540
Dermatologist, Song Eun-yeong.

59:03.623 --> 59:06.543
Former MCST Vice Minister, Kim Jeong-ho.

59:07.043 --> 59:09.212
Ilseong Pharmaceuticals CEO, Ko Tae-hyeon.

59:09.295 --> 59:11.506
Hyeonil Corporation CEO, Kim Sang-i.

59:11.589 --> 59:14.926
Bareun Bank Yeouido Branch Manager,
Kwon Min-ho.

59:17.428 --> 59:20.848
And lastly,
current member of the National Assembly,

59:21.432 --> 59:22.350
Lee Cheol-myeon.

59:22.433 --> 59:24.102
-Lee Cheol-myeon?
-Lee Cheol-myeon?

59:24.185 --> 59:25.353
-What?
-Really?

59:25.979 --> 59:28.106
-I think it's true.
-Hey, take photos.

59:28.189 --> 59:29.440
What are you trying to do?

59:29.524 --> 59:30.775
This is slander!

59:30.858 --> 59:32.694
-This is slander.
-It's slander!

59:32.777 --> 59:34.946
I'm going to sue you for defamation!

59:35.029 --> 59:36.030
Shut up!

59:36.656 --> 59:39.534
Or your damn child's face
will be all over the news.

59:45.123 --> 59:46.499
Are you not ashamed?

59:46.583 --> 59:49.627
Whenever your child's education
is discussed,

59:49.711 --> 59:51.796
why do you,
regardless of party or profession,

59:51.879 --> 59:53.923
cover your eyes, mouths, and ears,

59:55.341 --> 59:56.801
acting like fools?

59:57.594 --> 01:00:00.680
A teacher,
who should have been the fairest judge,

01:00:00.763 --> 01:00:03.474
pressured a student
from a difficult background

01:00:03.975 --> 01:00:07.562
and sabotaged their grades,
holding back their potential.

01:00:09.814 --> 01:00:11.316
How can you call him a teacher?

01:00:11.941 --> 01:00:15.153
Not everyone who is called a teacher
is truly a teacher.

01:00:16.946 --> 01:00:21.367
Did you say the ERPB is an organization
that only goes after children?

01:00:22.660 --> 01:00:26.789
Did you say we're now attacking teachers
only to avoid that allegation?

01:00:29.834 --> 01:00:31.002
You're wrong.

01:00:32.879 --> 01:00:37.216
The ERPB does not stand
with either the teachers or the students.

01:00:38.426 --> 01:00:40.053
We stand with the victims.

01:00:42.639 --> 01:00:45.224
The ERPB exists
for those who have suffered

01:00:45.308 --> 01:00:50.730
when a student or a teacher
could not live up to their role.

01:00:52.148 --> 01:00:54.359
If you call this a personal vendetta,
then it is.

01:00:54.859 --> 01:00:58.237
Someone needs to step up and take revenge
when the law fails.

01:00:58.738 --> 01:01:01.908
Only then can the victims
live their lives with peace of mind.

01:01:03.409 --> 01:01:06.287
I will find every person
who got into college unfairly

01:01:06.371 --> 01:01:09.540
and the adults who were party to that.

01:01:10.083 --> 01:01:11.292
I will find them all

01:01:12.001 --> 01:01:15.338
and show them
what real fairness looks like.

01:01:17.131 --> 01:01:22.512
I hope good teachers don't get called out
because of a few bad apples.

01:01:23.513 --> 01:01:24.347
Please

01:01:25.598 --> 01:01:27.517
act accordingly.

01:01:27.600 --> 01:01:29.435
Adults should act like adults

01:01:30.311 --> 01:01:32.105
and teachers like teachers.

01:01:44.867 --> 01:01:46.577
Jung Su-jeong, where are you?

01:01:47.078 --> 01:01:48.538
Hurry home already!

01:01:51.416 --> 01:01:53.668
And I'm saying this just in case.

01:01:53.751 --> 01:01:56.212
Don't even think about
trying to leave the country.

01:01:57.213 --> 01:01:59.298
You're all under a travel ban.

01:02:04.554 --> 01:02:08.057
Deputy Bong's equipment worked wonders.

01:02:08.141 --> 01:02:09.809
-It's a really expensive…
-Hey.

01:02:10.309 --> 01:02:12.937
-Should I carry that for you?
-No, I'm fine.

01:02:13.438 --> 01:02:15.106
-Teach him how to pack.
-Ma'am!

01:02:24.198 --> 01:02:25.408
Thank you.

01:02:36.794 --> 01:02:38.045
Thank you.

01:02:48.055 --> 01:02:49.807
Just do as you always have.

01:03:00.193 --> 01:03:01.486
-I recorded…
-So…

01:03:01.569 --> 01:03:04.697
What? Deputy Bong,
did you have something to say?

01:03:06.532 --> 01:03:07.658
No, it's nothing.

01:03:09.660 --> 01:03:11.913
Why are you crying, dude?

01:03:14.207 --> 01:03:16.083
You'd better head back and study.

01:03:16.167 --> 01:03:17.460
You've got this, right?

01:03:18.377 --> 01:03:19.337
Yes, sir.

01:03:25.968 --> 01:03:29.138
All you need to do now is study hard.
Good luck.

01:03:29.639 --> 01:03:33.184
Where did you get the list of the people
who manipulated the grades?

01:03:33.684 --> 01:03:36.813
I told each of them I'd let them off
if they gave me one name,

01:03:36.896 --> 01:03:37.980
and they all told me.

01:03:38.064 --> 01:03:38.898
Nice.

01:03:53.621 --> 01:03:56.916
All I did was buy him one cup of tea
during the consultation.

01:03:56.999 --> 01:03:59.585
We will speak when my attorney gets here!

01:03:59.669 --> 01:04:01.838
So what? I'm an assemblyman.
Don't touch me!

01:04:01.921 --> 01:04:03.297
Attorney Kang, where are you?

01:04:03.381 --> 01:04:05.716
-Why the hell aren't you here already?
-Please sit.

01:04:25.695 --> 01:04:29.198
I want to show you
how you ruined a child's life.

01:06:31.737 --> 01:06:34.699
Subtitle translation by: Lisa Kim
